crifices::Sin Offering::reviewed_publisher_redirect","scope":"reviewed_publisher_redirect","senseReview":"The original publisher explicitly links this complete unambiguous name/phrase to this target. Redirect and target were reviewed once; actual BSB phrase and full word boundaries required. Target original title and complete article remain unchanged.","sourceHeadwordId":"SinOffering","term":"Sin Offering"},{"ruleId":"OfferingsandSacrifices::Drink Offering::reviewed_publisher_redirect","scope":"reviewed_publisher_redirect","senseReview":"The original publisher explicitly links this complete unambiguous name/phrase to this target. Redirect and target were reviewed once; actual BSB phrase and full word boundaries required. Target original title and complete article remain unchanged.","sourceHeadwordId":"DrinkOffering","term":"Drink Offering"}],"matchingRule":"source_verified_redirect","matchingRules":["source_verified_redirect"],"sourceProvenanceId":"OfferingsandSacrifices","sourceTitle":"Offerings and Sacrifices"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Num.28.1-29.40","r":"Num.28.1-29.40","rawR":"Num.28.1-29.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.28.1-29.40","value":"Num.28.1-29.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"28:1–29:40"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," These two chapters contain information about Israel’s ritual calendar, including a list of required daily, weekly, and monthly offerings and a list of annual religious events. Thus Israel was instructed to worship God “properly and in order” (",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.14.40","r":"1Cor.14.40","rawR":"1Cor.14.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.14.40","value":"1Cor.14.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 14:40"},"). The annual cycle of sacrifices involved a tremendous investment of animals, grain, oil, and wine. Israel marked these special days by stopping their normal work, a kind of sacrifice that recognized the importance of these holy days. This annual cycle included eight different occasions for worship, all of which recalled Israel’s relationship with the Lord. Each worship event included a different combination of burnt, grain, liquid, and/or sin offerings. • For details on the grain and liquid offerings, see ",{"href":"?bref=Num.15.1-16","r":"Num.15.1-16","rawR":"Num.15.1-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.15.1-16","value":"Num.15.1-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Num 15:1-16"},". For explanations of the different types of offerings, see ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.1.1-7.38","r":"Lev.1.1-7.38","rawR":"Lev.1.1-7.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.1.1-7.38","value":"Lev.1.1-7.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lev 1:1–7:38"},". For a description of Israel’s festivals, see ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.23.1-44","r":"Lev.23.1-44","rawR":"Lev.23.1-44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.23.1-44","value":"Lev.23.1-44"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lev 23:1-44"},". For the New Testament perspective on the Old Testament sacrificial system, see ",{"href":"?bref=John.1.29","r":"John.1.29","rawR":"John.1.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.1.29","value":"John.1.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"John 1:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rom.12.1","r":"Rom.12.1","rawR":"Rom.12.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.12.1","value":"Rom.12.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 12:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.9.9-15","r":"Heb.9.9-15","rawR":"Heb.9.9-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.9.9-15","value":"Heb.9.9-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 9:9-15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.10.1-2","r":"Heb.10.1-2","rawR":"Heb.10.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.10.1-2","value":"Heb.10.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:1-2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Pet.2.5","r":"1Pet.2.5","rawR":"1Pet.2.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Pet.2.5","value":"1Pet.2.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Pet 2:5"},"."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Num.28.1-29.40","refs":[{"book":"NUM","endChapter":29,"endVerse":40,"startChapter":28,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Num.28.1-29.40","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"NUM","sourceChapterCoverage":[28,29],"sourceItemFragmentS